@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product] shared-home-keeps-production-state
The Inbox's Compose state, list synchronization, archive, tour index, sort and folds
MUST use one production implementation on Android and iOS. Native storage, source
identity, clocks and first-party analytics MUST enter through the existing store and
small service interfaces. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS decision.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] shared-home-cache-and-policies-stay-compatible
The device list MUST show before server cache and fresh data. An old request MUST NOT
replace a newer selection or list. Existing preference keys, JSON formats, archive
head-based restoration, hidden-repository filtering, stable sorts and Jev grouping
MUST remain compatible. The archive MUST keep at most 500 entries, the tour index 60
and dismissed task IDs 100; the separate persisted tour cache keeps its existing 200
budget. Source: the accepted 21 Oct iOS reuse plan; DESIGN.md rules 51, 53, 56, 111,
114, 118, 190 and 202 and existing HomeLogic/InboxLogic behavior.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] shared-home-state-belongs-to-source
Private Inbox copies and tour/archive records MUST belong to one native server/account/
authorization source. Invalid configuration MUST bypass persistence. A source change MUST clear old
reactive state and deny late writes, results or reconciliation; no raw credentials MAY
become a persistence namespace. Legacy records without provable ownership MUST NOT
be adopted as another account's data. Source: the accepted 21 Oct iOS persistence and
source-identity plan, preserving the review-session source boundary.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-home-observation-keeps-authority
A source invalidated while a refresh/classification interval waits MUST NOT start the
next request against a different source. Unknown tour-task snapshots MUST NOT settle
or erase an unfinished row; later known done, failed or cancelled snapshots MAY settle
it, with the existing stale-writing expiry unchanged. Source: the accepted 21 Oct iOS
source-identity plan and the shared authoritative-task outcome policy.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] shared-home-screen-caches-have-an-owner
Repository first pages, posted diffs and profile numbers MUST belong to an explicit
native source owner. A source change MUST clear reactive copies and reject late results
and writes; another account or Access context MUST NOT inherit a private copy. Memory
first-page caches MUST be bounded, while existing JSON, preference keys and the separate
200-tour file budget remain compatible. Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS plan
and its native persistence/source-identity boundary.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product] shared-home-requires-native-actions
Shared Home and repository screens MUST receive native clipboard, external GitHub,
explicit-browser and lifecycle actions. These services MUST NOT be silently replaced
by inert callbacks. Native lifecycle registration MUST report the current foreground
state once and observe later start, resume and stop events until cancelled. Source:
Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS plan: shared production screens with thin native adapters.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-home-input-and-ask-follow-source
Ordinary route navigation MUST retain the Inbox's filter, scroll and private input.
Changing its server/account/authorization owner MUST clear private search and Ask-open
state and cancel its old Ask scope before another request can start. Source: the
accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS source-ownership plan and DESIGN.md rule 118.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-private-screen-state-follows-owner
Home and repository private hold cards, sheet input and saveable searches MUST belong
to the screen's source owner. The same owner MUST restore ordinary route state; a new
owner MUST NOT restore old private input, including when the route was offscreen during
the source change. Native first-screen size hints MUST use that same owner's revocable
lease; a late old writer MUST NOT refill or clear the current source. Source: the
accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS source-ownership and shared-navigation plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] shared-home-stale-actions-cannot-cross-source
A resource-opening or Ask callback retained from an invalidated source MUST NOT
navigate or start work under replacement credentials. Back and Home MAY still clean
up the existing route stack. Renderer capability gates MUST remain enforced for the
current owner. Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026 iOS source-ownership plan and existing
shared Home observation and private-state boundaries.
Press-to-warm MUST apply that same current-owner and renderer gate before the
application cache captures a client source; an old row MUST NOT preload through
replacement credentials. Source: the independent 21 Oct 2026 PR80 source review.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] shared-native-reader-effects-belong-to-the-current-source
Native clipboard, browser and lifecycle callbacks retained by a private reader MUST
reject its retired account/server/Access owner. Native recognition MUST remain one
root observer; source cancellation MAY clear a gesture but MUST NOT commit work for
replacement credentials. Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 source-isolated iOS
root and maximum-reuse native-services plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product] shared-relative-dates-use-the-app-language
The shared relative-date formatter MUST keep the existing relativeTime unit and
rounding policy and format its result in the app's selected language through native
locale services. Android MUST retain its original ICU behavior; iOS MUST support
named relative dates without a separate maintained translation table. Source: Tavi's
21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS plan and the existing locale source-of-truth policy.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product] shared-home-settings-does-not-imply-ui-book-readiness
The Home host MUST advertise Settings and UI Book route readiness independently.
Installing the actual Settings sheet MUST NOT enable a missing UI Book renderer;
Android MUST retain its existing complete UI Book route. Source: Tavi's accepted
21 Oct 2026 per-renderer readiness and maximum-reuse iOS implementation plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] home-observation-is-a-revocable-read-lifetime
Native backgrounding, source retirement and pending account verification MUST stop
Home task/list/saved-result observations without a composition frame or a remote
task cancellation. Resuming MUST restart reads for the current verified source;
an earlier or cancellation-resistant result MUST NOT publish after a pause/resume
cycle. Accepted writes MUST remain outside this disposable read lifetime. Source:
Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 foreground/resume iOS plan and shared Home source policy.
When verification reopens that authority, the current mounted list/filter, task poll
and saved-result observers MUST restart without another native event or a user
refresh. An interrupted old selection MUST NOT replace the latest drawn selection.
Source: the independent 21 Oct 2026 native verification/read-restart review.
A repository's resumed first-page answer MUST restart an active search's remaining
page drain, including when the old search had already consumed every page. Source:
the independent 21 Oct 2026 repository resume/search review and current-filter rule.
A cancelled read's late network failure MUST NOT publish a new list/profile error,
become an ordinary unsuccessful refresh, or start its fallback request. Source:
the independent 21 Oct 2026 read-cancellation publication review.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] shared-inbox-ask-is-the-original-journey
Both hosts MUST use the original Inbox Ask transcript, known pull references, streaming
answer, merged work log, copy, redo, suggestions, stop and new-chat workflow through
the actual inbox/task RPCs. A busy existing server answer MUST keep a new question as
an unsent draft; a failed start MUST retain the current saved answer and unsent words.
Send MUST NOT erase words restored by an immediately rejected or reused-task reply,
and a newer draft entered during that request MUST remain intact.
Source: home-search-or-ask, DESIGN.md rule 99 and Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026
maximum-reuse iOS plan, applied to the original Android InboxAsk implementation.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-inbox-ask-keeps-source-and-drawn-controls
One Inbox Ask controller MUST belong to one captured Repo source. Its root MUST
synchronously erase draft, transcript, pending question, task and error references
before replacement credentials publish. A disposed, revoked or replaced conversation's
typing, question, redo, stop, clear, copy, link and dismissal callbacks MUST become
inert. Root and latest drawn host readiness MUST precede paid/control RPCs. Ordinary
sheet dismissal MUST retain the same source's conversation and draft. Source: the
accepted 21 Oct 2026 private-source ownership and complete Inbox Ask iOS plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-inbox-observation-does-not-invent-an-outcome
Background or sheet-disposal pauses MUST cancel only read/list/poll observation,
never an accepted start or clear write. After a paused write's receipt, fresh
conversation/list/poll reads MUST wait for an eligible observer; a reused task's
unsent question MUST reconcile then without replacing a newer draft. Connection
loss, unknown/mismatched task snapshots and missing observations MUST NOT invent
remote failure, completion or cancellation. They MUST preserve the accepted task, offer observation retry, and
resume from matching non-regressing authoritative task or saved-conversation data.
Old source or operation replies MUST NOT populate the replacement. Source: the
accepted 21 Oct 2026 Inbox Ask pause/resume and authoritative-task iOS plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] shared-inbox-verification-and-native-foreground-are-independent
The source verification gate MUST pause Inbox reads synchronously without rewriting
the actual native lifecycle. Resumed sheet observation and retained sheet controls
MUST require both a ready gate and an actually foreground mounted reader. Accepted
server writes MUST keep their separate source lifetime. Source: the accepted
21 Oct 2026 verified-source and Inbox pause/resume iOS plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] shared-inbox-stop-keeps-a-rejected-task-running
An explicit Inbox Ask Stop MUST require a successful server cancellation receipt;
rejection MUST retain the authoritative running task and expose its error for retry.
A visible eligible reader MUST receive the existing Error feedback. An accepted
same-source rejection MUST remain readable after ordinary dismissal or pause without
replaying feedback on resume; a retired source or replacement operation MUST NOT
receive it. A queued Stop MUST recheck its drawn control before dispatch. Cleanup
cancellation MUST retain its existing best-effort behavior. Source: Tavi's accepted
22 Oct 2026 complete native AI Stop/error journey and the real RPC rejection review.
Only the latest actually dispatched explicit Stop for the still-running Inbox task
MAY publish a rejection; an unsent queued tap MUST NOT supersede an accepted receipt.
Source: the accepted 22 Oct 2026 full Stop receipt-ordering review, finding 1.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;product] home-write-dispatch-requires-current-verified-readiness
Posted deletion and an explicit running-tour Stop MUST check the current source and
verified foreground readiness before sending a new write, including a retained or
queued callback. An accepted same-source receipt MUST still settle after an ordinary
scene pause; a replacement source MUST NOT receive its rows, cues or errors. A failed
or unstarted Stop MUST NOT announce that the tour stopped. Source: Tavi's accepted
21 Oct 2026 full native review/AI journey and verified scene lifecycle plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] native-dialog-back-authority-belongs-to-its-host-and-source
A native Dialog Back bridge MUST use the host's real active-scene/root/presentation
authority. A source-bound native adapter MUST additionally reject a retired source,
and a host which provides no authority MUST fail closed. The adapter MUST NOT install
a second recognizer or infer native foreground from server verification. Source: the
accepted 22 Oct 2026 actual limitation-sheet Back completion repair, preserving
shared-inbox-verification-and-native-foreground-are-independent.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] home-first-load-shows-rows-as-they-arrive
With nothing on screen, the Inbox MUST show the rows the server's first load has found so
far while the whole list is still coming, ending in a few skeleton rows and never in the
empty note, instead of skeletons until every pull request is in. Those rows MUST NOT
